Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:16:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Shaders: ds_bpermute_b32 reads within the lane's 32-lane half

GFX10 runs ds_bpermute_b32 on each half of a wave of 64 on its own:
lane l reads lane (l & 32) | (address / 4 & 31). LLVM says so
(supportsWaveWideBPermute is false for GFX10 and GFX11 in wave64), and
so does Mesa's ACO ("ds_bpermute is restricted to 32 lanes on
GFX10-GFX11.7").

The translation read lane (address / 4 & 63): on 64-lane hosts a lane
naming the other half read it, and on 32-lane hosts the program was
refused as a permute across two host waves. It now reads within the
half in both forms, and ds_bpermute no longer makes a console wave64
program exchange between its host waves.
